  "query": "Error message handling for notifications still needs work\nhttps://github.com/tuskyapp/Tusky/pull/3440 displayed error text when notifications fail to load because of the server, but the presentation of that can still be improved. I caught an error from mastodon.social a moment ago, and it currently looks like this:\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/773100/224696114-f41bcd30-fcb2-42ca-9ed4-3ca1487fb1d4.png\" width=\"60%\">\r\n\r\nThat's obviously a JSON representation of the error. That's lead me to https://docs.joinmastodon.org/entities/Error/, so the right thing to do here is probably to decode this and present the error to user. Probably as:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<http error code>: <error>\r\n\r\n<error description>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI want to avoid hiding this info behind a generic \"An error occurred\" message because it makes it impossible to troubleshoot user reports of problems.\n",
